            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used homemade applesauce in this recipe and omitted the sugar. I served these up like pancakes with homemade apple cider syrup. The family LOVED these. VERY filling.",
            "datePublished": "2012-10-18T05:52:50.850Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kirk Gonzalez"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My family loved this. I replaced the raisins with blueberries. (I add them after mixing the batter well, then put in the blueberries and softly stir.) They are so soft and moist that my mother-in-law can also enjoy them even though it's hard for her to eat most foods. I also use a good deal of powdered sugar and skip the syrup.",
            "datePublished": "2009-10-09T09:36:59.303Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
